    "text_frames": [
      {
        "id": "notes",
        "position": [
          2,
          1
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**CT07 \u2014 How much gain or phase reserve does this loop have?**  \n**Predict \u2192 Run \u2192 Inspect \u2192 Change gain.** Run 64 s at 10 Hz. Open Frequency response: Bode and Nyquist. Gain reference must be 1; keep phase unwrapped.  \nL(z)=0.01K/(z\u22120.9)\u00b2. At K=4, gain margin=19/4; at K=16, 19/16. DC is excluded from the log-frequency Bode plot, but retained in Nyquist/export.  \nSelect gain, F4: value 4 \u2192 16; save/reopen/rerun. All signals use normalized unit 1.  \nSource/state sample n is observed at Scope time (n+1)/10 s. Each lag updates from the same old states; do not add a feedback delay.  \n[Open CT07 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/CT07-stability-margins/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT root locus](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/16-06-principles-of-automatic-control-fall-2012/resources/mit16_06f12_lecture_11/) \u00b7 [MIT stability margins](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/16-06-principles-of-automatic-control-fall-2012/resources/mit16_06f12_lecture_23/)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1700,
          "height": 440,
          "font_size": 20
        }
      }
    ]
